{"type":"message","id":"c564bd4f","parentId":"2a623475","timestamp":"2026-02-20T09:18:36.232Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"skills-config.md를 읽어보겠습니다.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_48ccd64cfde547cfabea204d","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/skills-config.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":310,"output":60,"cacheRead":39318,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":39688,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771579114205}}
{"type":"message","id":"478cb5b6","parentId":"c564bd4f","timestamp":"2026-02-20T09:18:36.239Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_48ccd64cfde547cfabea204d","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nsummary: \"Skills config schema and examples\"\nread_when:\n  - Adding or modifying skills config\n  - Adjusting bundled allowlist or install behavior\ntitle: \"Skills Config\"\n---\n\n# Skills Config\n\nAll skills-related configuration lives under `skills` in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`.\n\n```json5\n{\n  skills: {\n    allowBundled: [\"gemini\", \"peekaboo\"],\n    load: {\n      extraDirs: [\"~/Projects/agent-scripts/skills\", \"~/Projects/oss/some-skill-pack/skills\"],\n      watch: true,\n      watchDebounceMs: 250,\n    },\n    install: {\n      preferBrew: true,\n      nodeManager: \"npm\", // npm | pnpm | yarn | bun (Gateway runtime still Node; bun not recommended)\n    },\n    entries: {\n      \"nano-banana-pro\": {\n        enabled: true,\n        apiKey: \"GEMINI_KEY_HERE\",\n        env: {\n          GEMINI_API_KEY: \"GEMINI_KEY_HERE\",\n        },\n      },\n      peekaboo: { enabled: true },\n      sag: { enabled: false },\n    },\n  },\n}\n```\n\n## Fields\n\n- `allowBundled`: optional allowlist for **bundled** skills only. When set, only\n  bundled skills in the list are eligible (managed/workspace skills unaffected).\n- `load.extraDirs`: additional skill directories to scan (lowest precedence).\n- `load.watch`: watch skill folders and refresh the skills snapshot (default: true).\n- `load.watchDebounceMs`: debounce for skill watcher events in milliseconds (default: 250).\n- `install.preferBrew`: prefer brew installers when available (default: true).\n- `install.nodeManager`: node installer preference (`npm` | `pnpm` | `yarn` | `bun`, default: npm).\n  This only affects **skill installs**; the Gateway runtime should still be Node\n  (Bun not recommended for WhatsApp/Telegram).\n- `entries.<skillKey>`: per-skill overrides.\n\nPer-skill fields:\n\n- `enabled`: set `false` to disable a skill even if it’s bundled/installed.\n- `env`: environment variables injected for the agent run (only if not already set).\n- `apiKey`: optional convenience for skills that declare a primary env var.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Keys under `entries` map to the skill name by default. If a skill defines\n  `metadata.openclaw.skillKey`, use that key instead.\n- Changes to skills are picked up on the next agent turn when the watcher is enabled.\n\n### Sandboxed skills + env vars\n\nWhen a session is **sandboxed**, skill processes run inside Docker. The sandbox\ndoes **not** inherit the host `process.env`.\n\nUse one of:\n\n- `agents.defaults.sandbox.docker.env` (or per-agent `agents.list[].sandbox.docker.env`)\n- bake the env into your custom sandbox image\n\nGlobal `env` and `skills.entries.<skill>.env/apiKey` apply to **host** runs only.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771579116235}}
{"type":"message","id":"70a98641","parentId":"478cb5b6","timestamp":"2026-02-20T09:18:39.231Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"여기에는 nativeSkills에 대한 설명이 없습니다. commands 관련 문서를 찾아봐야 할 것 같습니다.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4e1ba993e5304e5ea33d4230","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r \"commands\" ~/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs --include=\"*.md\" | grep -i \"native\" | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":643,"output":112,"cacheRead":39675,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":40430,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771579116239}}
{"type":"message","id":"1529718f","parentId":"70a98641","timestamp":"2026-02-20T09:18:39.265Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4e1ba993e5304e5ea33d4230","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:    native: \"auto\", // register native commands when supported\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:- `native: \"auto\"` turns on native commands for Discord/Telegram, leaves Slack off.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:- Override per channel: `channels.discord.commands.native` (bool or `\"auto\"`). `false` clears previously registered commands.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:summary: \"Slash commands: text vs native, config, and supported commands\"\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:  - On surfaces without native commands (WhatsApp/WebChat/Signal/iMessage/Google Chat/MS Teams), text commands still work even if you set this to `false`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:- `commands.native` (default `\"auto\"`) registers native commands.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:  - Auto: on for Discord/Telegram; off for Slack (until you add slash commands); ignored for providers without native support.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:  - Set `channels.discord.commands.native`, `channels.telegram.commands.native`, or `channels.slack.commands.native` to override per provider (bool or `\"auto\"`).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:- `commands.nativeSkills` (default `\"auto\"`) registers **skill** commands natively when supported.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:  - Set `channels.discord.commands.nativeSkills`, `channels.telegram.commands.nativeSkills`, or `channels.slack.commands.nativeSkills` to override per provider (bool or `\"auto\"`).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:  - `/skill <name> [input]` runs a skill by name (useful when native command limits prevent per-skill commands).\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:- **Native commands** use isolated sessions:\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:- **Slack:** `channels.slack.slashCommand` is still supported for a single `/openclaw`-style command. If you enable `commands.native`, you must create one Slack slash command per built-in command (same names as `/help`). Command argument menus for Slack are delivered as ephemeral Block Kit buttons.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/plugin.md:- `actions` (message actions), `commands` (native command behavior)\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/configuration.md:- `commands.native: \"auto\"`（默认）为 Discord/Telegram 启用原生命令，Slack 保持关闭；不支持的渠道保持纯文本。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/gateway/configuration.md:- 设为 `commands.native: true|false` 强制全部开启或关闭，或按渠道覆盖 `channels.discord.commands.native`、`channels.telegram.commands.native`、`channels.slack.commands.native`（bool 或 `\"auto\"`）。`false` 在启动时清除 Discord/Telegram 上先前注册的命令；Slack 命令在 Slack 应用中管理。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/tools/slash-commands.md:- `commands.native`（默认 `\"auto\"`）注册原生命令。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/tools/slash-commands.md:  - 设置 `channels.discord.commands.native`、`channels.telegram.commands.native` 或 `channels.slack.commands.native` 以按提供商覆盖（布尔值或 `\"auto\"`）。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/tools/slash-commands.md:- `commands.nativeSkills`（默认 `\"auto\"`）在支持时原生注册 **Skill** 命令。\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/zh-CN/tools/slash-commands.md:  - 设置 `channels.discord.commands.nativeSkills`、`channels.telegram.commands.nativeSkills` 或 `channels.slack.commands.nativeSkills` 以按提供商覆盖（布尔值或 `\"auto\"`）。"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":27,"aggregated":"/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:    native: \"auto\", // register native commands when supported\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:- `native: \"auto\"` turns on native commands for Discord/Telegram, leaves Slack off.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/gateway/configuration-reference.md:- Override per channel: `channels.discord.commands.native` (bool or `\"auto\"`). `false` clears previously registered commands.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:summary: \"Slash commands: text vs native, config, and supported commands\"\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:  - On surfaces without native commands (WhatsApp/WebChat/Signal/iMessage/Google Chat/MS Teams), text commands still work even if you set this to `false`.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:- `commands.native` (default `\"auto\"`) registers native commands.\n/home/lfant/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/lib/node_modules/openclaw/docs/tools/slash-commands.md:  - Auto: on for Discord/Telegram;