{"type":"message","id":"e6cfd22e","parentId":"3520ff2f","timestamp":"2026-02-20T09:42:11.697Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9a6de6f2a3e145b98a68d2ed","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Usage: gog auth add <email> [flags]\nBuild: v0.11.0 (91c4c15)\n\nAuthorize and store a refresh token\n\nArguments:\n  <email>    Email\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help                  Show context-sensitive help.\n      --color=\"auto\"          Color output: auto|always|never\n  -a, --account=STRING        Account email for API commands\n                              (gmail/calendar/chat/classroom/drive/docs/slides/contacts/tasks/people/sheets/forms/appscript)\n      --client=\"\"             OAuth client name (selects stored credentials +\n                              token bucket)\n      --enable-commands=\"\"    Comma-separated list of enabled top-level commands\n                              (restricts CLI)\n  -j, --json                  Output JSON to stdout (best for scripting)\n  -p, --plain                 Output stable, parseable text to stdout (TSV;\n                              no colors)\n      --results-only          In JSON mode, emit only the primary result (drops\n                              envelope fields like nextPageToken)\n      --select=STRING         In JSON mode, select comma-separated fields\n                              (best-effort; supports dot paths). Desire path:\n                              use --fields for most commands.\n  -n, --dry-run               Do not make changes; print intended actions and\n                              exit successfully\n  -y, --force                 Skip confirmations for destructive commands\n      --no-input              Never prompt; fail instead (useful for CI)\n  -v, --verbose               Enable verbose logging\n      --version               Print version and exit\n\n      --manual                Browserless auth flow (paste redirect URL)\n      --remote                Remote/server-friendly manual flow (print URL,\n                              then exchange code)\n      --step=INT              Remote auth step: 1=print URL, 2=exchange code\n      --auth-url=STRING       Redirect URL from browser (manual flow; required\n                              for --remote --step 2)\n      --timeout=DURATION      Authorization timeout (manual flows default to 5m)\n      --force-consent         Force consent screen to obtain a refresh token\n      --services=\"user\"       Services to authorize: user|all or comma-separated\n                              gmail,calendar,chat,classroom,drive,docs,slides,contacts,tasks,sheets,people,forms,appscript\n                              (Keep uses service account: gog auth\n                              service-account set)\n      --readonly              Use read-only scopes where available (still\n                              includes OIDC identity scopes)\n      --drive-scope=\"full\"    Drive scope mode: full|readonly|file"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":23,"aggregated":"Usage: gog auth add <email> [flags]\nBuild: v0.11.0 (91c4c15)\n\nAuthorize and store a refresh token\n\nArguments:\n  <email>    Email\n\nFlags:\n  -h, --help                  Show context-sensitive help.\n      --color=\"auto\"          Color output: auto|always|never\n  -a, --account=STRING        Account email for API commands\n                              (gmail/calendar/chat/classroom/drive/docs/slides/contacts/tasks/people/sheets/forms/appscript)\n      --client=\"\"             OAuth client name (selects stored credentials +\n                              token bucket)\n      --enable-commands=\"\"    Comma-separated list of enabled top-level commands\n                              (restricts CLI)\n  -j, --json                  Output JSON to stdout (best for scripting)\n  -p, --plain                 Output stable, parseable text to stdout (TSV;\n                              no colors)\n      --results-only          In JSON mode, emit only the primary result (drops\n                              envelope fields like nextPageToken)\n      --select=STRING         In JSON mode, select comma-separated fields\n                              (best-effort; supports dot paths). Desire path:\n                              use --fields for most commands.\n  -n, --dry-run               Do not make changes; print intended actions and\n                              exit successfully\n  -y, --force                 Skip confirmations for destructive commands\n      --no-input              Never prompt; fail instead (useful for CI)\n  -v, --verbose               Enable verbose logging\n      --version               Print version and exit\n\n      --manual                Browserless auth flow (paste redirect URL)\n      --remote                Remote/server-friendly manual flow (print URL,\n                              then exchange code)\n      --step=INT              Remote auth step: 1=print URL, 2=exchange code\n      --auth-url=STRING       Redirect URL from browser (manual flow; required\n                              for --remote --step 2)\n      --timeout=DURATION      Authorization timeout (manual flows default to 5m)\n      --force-consent         Force consent screen to obtain a refresh token\n      --services=\"user\"       Services to authorize: user|all or comma-separated\n                              gmail,calendar,chat,classroom,drive,docs,slides,contacts,tasks,sheets,people,forms,appscript\n                              (Keep uses service account: gog auth\n                              service-account set)\n      --readonly              Use read-only scopes where available (still\n                              includes OIDC identity scopes)\n      --drive-scope=\"full\"    Drive scope mode: full|readonly|file","cwd":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1771580531691}}
