{"type":"message","id":"56ea5e6b","parentId":"dfc50dcf","timestamp":"2026-02-20T16:38:10.085Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_ppP2kFg1Ix5LJzxd26FniOda|fc_048b45c3663fe2170169988df3fad08191815699afad6143d1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\nThink of it like a human reviewing their journal and updating their mental model. Daily files are raw notes; MEMORY.md is curated wisdom.\n\nThe goal: Be helpful without being annoying. Check in a few times a day, do useful background work, but respect quiet time.\n\n## 🧠 Model Routing Rule (Main vs Sub-Agent)\n\nUse this routing policy by default:\n\n- **Main session:** fast/default work on **GLM-4.7**\n- **Sub-agent:** complex reasoning/coding work on **Codex (gpt-5.3-codex, thinking=high)**\n\n### When to escalate to a sub-agent (Codex)\n\nEscalate when one or more apply:\n\n1. Multi-step reasoning with dependencies (plan → verify → revise)\n2. Code changes across multiple files/modules\n3. Deep debugging / root-cause analysis with hypothesis testing\n4. Security/compliance trade-off decisions (blast radius, risk analysis)\n5. Long-running research/synthesis tasks likely to block main conversation\n\n### When to stay in main session (GLM)\n\nStay in main when tasks are:\n\n- quick Q&A or summaries\n- simple rewrites/formatting\n- one-shot checks with low ambiguity\n- low-risk operational confirmations\n\n### Execution default\n\n- Prefer spawning sub-agents for complex tasks.\n- Sub-agent defaults are configured to Codex + high thinking.\n- If needed, override per run explicitly with `sessions_spawn.model`.\n\n## Make It Yours\n\nThis is a starting point. Add your own conventions, style, and rules as you figure out what works.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771605490078}}
